kg:note_ref10074_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    crm:P72_has_language lang:und ;
    rdf:value "\"The Madrasa/mosque complex was built in 1866 on the orders of Mirza Mohammad Khan (Sipahsalar) (d.1867), Nasir al-Din shah's minister of the army and later chief minister. The complex includes also a library, bath, and hospital. The view is from atop the walls of the Mosque's courtyards showing the shops (Fabric sellers).\" [Freer Gallery of Art and Arthur M. Sackler Gallery Archives, Curatorial Research Assistant]" .

