kg:note_ref10110_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    crm:P72_has_language lang:und ;
    rdf:value "\"The gate pictured here might also be Darvaza-i Rah-Ahan (Gate of the Train). The photo should have been taken on the earlier days of railway construction betwen Tehran and Shah Abdul 'Azim by a Belgian engineer, M. Buvatal. The first line was constructed between Khurasan gate and Shah Abd al-'Azim gate in 1882. The steam coming out of the train was the reason behind the local naming of the train as Mashin Doodi (Smoking Machine).\" [Freer Gallery of Art and Arthur M. Sackler Gallery Archives, Curatorial Research Assistant]" .

