kg:note_ref10214_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    crm:P72_has_language lang:und ;
    rdf:value "\"The photo is most probably taken during the reign of Ahmad Shah Qajar and before the abolishment of Qajar dynasty. Boris Shumiatsky was in Iran from 1923 to 1925 and in this photo he is sitting beside Riza Khan. The style of ministers' headgears in the photo also indicates that the date is before 1926 when the Pahlavi Hats became mandatory for office workers. Therefore, it is safe to assume that the photo is taken around 1924.The man wearing glasses and standing towards the right side of the photo is Nusrat al-Dawla, the minister of Justice.\" [Freer Gallery of Art and Arthur M. Sackler Gallery Archives, Curatorial Research Assistant]" .

kg:note_ref10214_scopecontent_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    crm:P72_has_language lang:und ;
    rdf:value "- Handwritten information on slip of paper (from a 1943-1944 cash book, produced by the Bathni Brothers, Tehran) reads, \"300) Commercial treaty Iranian ministers.\" [Myron Bement Smith Collection, Subseries 2.1: Islamic Archives History, Collection Information]" .

kg:note_ref10214_scopecontent_2_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    crm:P72_has_language lang:und ;
