    rdf:value "\"The photo is of a stone-paste dish painted over glaze with luster, attributed to Kashan (Iran) of 1210 and in the Seljuq period. One of the inscriptions records that the plate was made by Shamsuddin al-Hasani Abu Zayd, an accomplished potter of the early thirteenth century. It is currently in collection of Freer|Sackler, the Smithsonian's museums of Asian art (F1941.11).\" [Freer Gallery of Art and Arthur M. Sackler Gallery Archives, Curatorial Research Assistant]" .

