kg:note_ref10315_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    crm:P72_has_language lang:und ;
    rdf:value "\"He is Muzaffar al-Din Shah's son and was appointed as the governor of Kermanshah in 1897. He was later removed from his post as the governor of Kermanshah due to people's dissatisfaction with his rule. Salar al-Dawla was later appointed to the government of Zanjan, Khuzestan, Bakhtiari and Brujird. After an unsuccessful coup against his brother - the crown prince Muhammad Ali Shah - in 1929 he was arrested and brought to Tehran. After many unsuccessful attempt to replace his brother as the next Qajar king, he fled to Europe and stayed there until his death in 1958.\" [Freer Gallery of Art and Arthur M. Sackler Gallery Archives, Curatorial Research Assistant]" .

