kg:note_ref10362_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    crm:P72_has_language lang:und ;
    rdf:value "\"Bahram Gur Hunts with Azada, Folio from the Great Il-Khanid Shahnama. The photo is of the lower part of a folio in Great Il-Khanid Shahnama. As can be seen in its margins, on the day the photo was taken the folio has been part of a binding. Also, the painting in the photograph has a few blemishes that currently do not exist on the object. The manuscript is dated to mid Fourteen century and to the current northwestern border region of Iran and the city of Tabriz. The photograph is of the painting alone, the page containing the painting is accompanied by the text of the poem in the folio. The folio is currently held in Harvard Art Museum (1957.193). The story the miniature of which is depicted in the photo has been a rather popular one, used as decoration of pottery and metalwork.\" [Freer Gallery of Art and Arthur M. Sackler Gallery Archives, Curatorial Research Assistant]" .

kg:note_ref10362_scopecontent_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    crm:P72_has_language lang:und ;
    rdf:value "- Myron Bement Smith handwritten caption in English reads, \"47.P; Box 40.7: Painting.\" [Myron Bement Smith Collection, Subseries 2.1: Islamic Archives History, Collection Information; Box 60; Folder 44: 47 P: Antoine Sevruguin, glass negatives, Iran]" .

