kg:note_ref10206_scopecontent_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Scope and Contents" ;
    crm:P148_has_component kg:note_ref10206_scopecontent_0_p_0 ;
    crm:P2_has_type mbs:ScopeContent ;
    crm:P72_has_language lang:und ;
    rdf:value "Scope and Contents \"The figure standing off-centre of the image to the right is Mostawfi al-Mamalik. Born in 1875, he inherited his father's title and official post as the chief of treasury when he was only 10. He left Iran for Paris in 1900 and came back in 1907 to accept the new role of minister of army in Amin al-Sultan's cabinet. In later years, he was repeatedly appointed as prime minster or the minister of army until he passed away in 1932.\" [Freer Gallery of Art and Arthur M. Sackler Gallery Archives, Curatorial Research Assistant]" ;
    mbs:noteType mbs:ScopeContent .

