kg:note_ref10301_scopecontent_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Scope and Contents" ;
    crm:P148_has_component kg:note_ref10301_scopecontent_0_p_0 ;
    crm:P2_has_type mbs:ScopeContent ;
    crm:P72_has_language lang:und ;
    rdf:value "Scope and Contents \"Naqsh-i Rustam, Open-Air fire altars, Western End of the site. The Negative is broken on both sides. The negative is related to 39.4. The arrangement of shadows and the position of the camera is identical in both images, suggesting that they are variation of the same photo on the same day. Unlike 39.4, this image does not include the figure of the bystander, commonly used in archeological photography for the purpose of sizing.\" [Freer Gallery of Art and Arthur M. Sackler Gallery Archives, Curatorial Research Assistant]" ;
    mbs:noteType mbs:ScopeContent .

