        "Scope and Contents - FSg curatorial research specialist remark on Antoin Sevruguin photo manipulation reads, \"Black paper stuck to this four sides of the image. The faces are all varnished and toned.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten information on slip of paper (from a 1943-1944 cash book, produced by the Bathni Brothers, Tehran) reads, \"303) A zoroastrian Family. [Marked with unidentified seal].\" [Myron Bement Smith Collection, Subseries 2.1: Islamic Archives History, Collection Information]",
        "Scope and Contents - Myron Bement Smith handwritten caption in English reads, \"47.P; Box 27.11: a zoroastrian Family (# 303).\" [Myron Bement Smith Collection, Subseries 2.1: Islamic Archives History, Collection Information; Box 60; Folder 44: 47 P: Antoine Sevruguin, glass negatives, Iran]" ;
